  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Consider a game of chance with $5$ prizes ($$0$, $$2$, $$3$, $$5$, and $$10$) where each outcome has a specific probability of happening, shown in the table below. \n\n| $\\text{Number}$ | $\\text{Probability}$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $$0$ | $10%$ |\n| $$2$ | $25%$ |\n| $$3$ | $30%$ |\n| $$5$ | $20%$ |\n| $$10$ | $15%$ |\n\nWhat is the expected profit per game?\n\nThe expected profit is $$$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let $p$ represent the profit on a single game, in dollars. Using the given probabilities, let's summarize this in a table.  If $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{1}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{10}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $p$ | $0$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ | $10$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[p] & =0\\cdot f(0)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{10})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{3}{10})+5(\\frac{1}{5})+10(\\frac{3}{20}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{9}{10}+1+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{9}{10}+\\frac{10}{10}+\\frac{15}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{10} \\\\  & =3.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $$\\,3.9.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
